  "body": "This PR does item 2 of #3461 only: the per-post rows of the conformance and comment-escape tests. Items 1, 3 and 4 stay open on the issue. Thus the PR ends with `Refs #3461`, not `Fixes`.\n\n## What changed\n- `crates/app/tests/conformance.rs` has no table with one row for each post. The tables `POSTS`, `LATHE_POSTS`, `PLASMA_POSTS`, `WIRE_POSTS`, `SINKER_POSTS` and `EXTENSIONS` are removed.\n- The rows come from `posting::BUILTINS` and the four family lists of `posting.rs`. A milling dialect is each registry entry that no family lists, except Klartext. Fanuc's goldens stay at the top of `golden/nc/`.\n- The extension check reads each post's own `extension = \"...\"` manifest line. Each post must declare `nc`, except the seven posts in the sorted table `NOT_NC`. Each of these seven keeps its citation.\n- `every_builtin_registry_entry_compiles` now asserts a partition:\n  - the names are unique;\n  - each entry has a shipped `.cps` file;\n  - each family name is in `BUILTINS`;\n  - each entry is in exactly one family;\n  - Fanuc is entry 0.\n- `crates/post/tests/comment_escape.rs` counts the `.cps` files that it finds. It no longer compares with the fixed number 26.\n- `docs/decisions/3461-post-test-rows.md` records the choices and what was dropped.\n\nThe same 16 mill posts, in the same order, and the same lathe, plasma, wire and sinker posts are checked as before. No post, golden or stream changed.\n\n## Cause\nEach new post added rows at the end of shared tables in two test files. Two new-post branches therefore conflicted in `conformance.rs`. In `comment_escape.rs` both branches changed `26` to `27`. Git merges two identical changes with no conflict. The merged count was one too low, so main went red after the second merge.\n\n## Tests\n- Reproduction before the change (red). I made two branches off 470d1a27c. Each added one new mill post's test rows, as a new-post PR does today. `git merge-tree --write-tree` of the two heads gave `CONFLICT (content): Merge conflict in crates/app/tests/conformance.rs`. `comment_escape.rs` merged to the wrong count, 27.\n- After the change (green). The same row edit on this head finds no table in either file (`git diff` is empty). A new post changes neither file.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test conformance`: 7 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --test comment_escape`: 4 passed.\n- This change touches tests only. Thus no product test can start red. The pins are the four mutations below. Each mutation was put in, run, and then removed:\n  1. Fanuc's goldens read from a subdirectory: `every_builtin_posts_every_golden_byte_exact` is red (`golden/nc/fanuc/contour_disc_hole.nc: No such file`).\n  2. `mill_posts()` returns no post: `every_builtin_registry_entry_compiles` is red (`each registry entry is in exactly one family`).\n  3. The `richauto` row is removed from `NOT_NC`: `every_builtin_declares_its_controls_file_extension` is red (`richauto.cps declares the .nc extension`).\n  4. One post (`haas`) is skipped without a result: `header_notes_use_each_shipped_dialect_and_keep_the_full_surface_bound` is red (`every shipped text post writes both notes`).\n- Quick gate on the final head 4c5b49c45 (`cargo xtask gate quick --base 470d1a27c`): 2 steps, 0 failed (`post comment_escape (1 fn)`, `app suites: conformance`).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy lanes: `cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run` reports `heavy reach: 0 step(s) reached, 122 skipped`. The diff reaches no heavy lane.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone. `git diff --stat 470d1a27c HEAD -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"examples/**\"` is empty. The conformance suite posted every golden byte for byte on this head. I did not run `example_catalog`, because no post, toolpath or recorded program changed.\n\n## Not exercised\n- Items 1, 3 and 4 of #3461. `BUILTINS`, the `embedded()` match and the family lists in `posting.rs` still have one line for each post. Thus two new-post branches still conflict there. `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` is not changed.\n- The `cargo xtask merge-plan` test in \"Done means\" needs item 1, so this PR does not add it.\n- The base is 470d1a27c. After that, upstream/main got #4251 (holders). That merge changes none of these files, and `git merge-tree` with it is clean.\n\n## Overlaps\n- #2646 (Hurco WinMax post, draft, `needs-rework`, `conflicts`, `P6`) adds rows to `POSTS` and `EXTENSIONS` and changes the count to 27. These are the lines that this PR removes. I did not stack on it: it is a `feat` that merges only at a cut, and a stack would hold this tooling fix until then. When #2646 is refreshed, it drops those three hunks. The decision file has the reason.\n\nChangelog: none (test-only; no behaviour change)\n\nRefs #3461\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
